The first five classify mostly as false positives: landfill water/soil, wheat/rice stress experiments, and NHANES urinary biomarkers. One medicinal-plant paper has metals data, but it is a Rhazya stricta sample from a salt mine, not the queued salt/food occurrence target, so I’m treating it as a target-cell miss rather than creating a novel ingredient route from this fire.
